-- title:
--   Nonvanishing of partialⱼΦ̄_N at a unique centre with uniformiser
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and $k$ an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$, let $N \ge 1$ with $q \nmid N$, and let `data` be a `ModularPolynomialData N`, i.e. a monic $\Phi \in \mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ whose degree in the outer variable is the Dedekind $\psi$-value $\sum_{d \mid N,\ d \text{ squarefree}} N/d$ and which annihilates the pair of $q$-expansions $(j, j_N)$, the inner variable being substituted by $j$ and the outer by $j_N$. Write $F = k(\tilde\jmath, \tilde\jmath_N)$ for the $k$-subfield `modularFunctionFieldC k N` of the Laurent series field over $k$ generated by `jqModC k` and `jqNModC k N`, and let $\tilde\jmath =$ `jGeomGen k N`, $\tilde\jmath_N =$ `jNGeomGen k N` be these two generators. Let $v$ be a place of $F$ over $k$ — a proper valuation subring of $F$ containing $k$ whose ring is a principal ideal ring — with associated order function $\operatorname{ord}_v$, and let $c = (c_1, c_2) \in k \times k$. Assume: $c$ is a centre of $v$, i.e. $\operatorname{ord}_v(\tilde\jmath - c_1) > 0$ and $\operatorname{ord}_v(\tilde\jmath_N - c_2) > 0$; every place of $F$ over $k$ having $c$ as a centre equals $v$; and $\operatorname{ord}_v(\tilde\jmath_N - c_2) = 1$. Then, reducing the coefficients of $\Phi$ into $k$ and interchanging the two variables by `swapBivar`, the derivative with respect to the outer variable of the resulting polynomial, evaluated at outer variable $c_1$ and inner variable $c_2$, is nonzero; equivalently, $(\partial \bar\Phi/\partial X)(c_1, c_2) \neq 0$, the derivative being taken in the $\tilde\jmath$-variable.
--
--   In classical terms this says that a point $c$ of the affine plane model $\bar\Phi_N = 0$ of the level-$N$ fibre which carries a single place, and at which $\tilde\jmath_N - c_2$ is a uniformiser, is a simple point whose tangent line is not horizontal; it is the converse of the implications that nonvanishing of $\partial_Y \bar\Phi_N(c)$ forces uniqueness of the place centred at $c$ and makes $\tilde\jmath - c_1$ a uniformiser there. It is used in the construction of residue-disc chart data for prolongation tuples, notably by [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.IsModel.exists_chartData_of_isStrictFst`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.ProlongationTuple.IsModel.exists_chartData_of_isStrictFst) and `…_of_isStrictSnd`.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_derivative_swapBivar_evalEval_ne_zero_of_isCentreOf_unique_of_ord_jNGeomGen_sub_eq_one.lean

